;;; A query's `:goal` whose `(absent …)` is over a relation the program names
;;; nowhere else loads, and holds of everything —
;;; M1f **W78**, register row `W78/goal-absent-no-such-relation`, filed by S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and no candidate. The goal asks which guest
;;; has not paid, `(absent (payed ?g))`, where the program's relation is `paid`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; No declaration, fact, rule or hrule of the program names `payed`, so the
;;; `(absent …)` holds whatever the state holds: refused at load, at the pattern,
;;; one line, on every command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2). With `paid` the goal's one
;;; row is `?g = Bob`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: the program loads, and the goal has two rows, `?g = Ann` and
;;; `?g = Bob`: Ann, who has paid, is answered as one who has not, exit 0 on every
;;; command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.11 (T1f.7.11.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (and (is-a ?g Guest) (absent (payed ?g))))
